    "result_text": "All 283 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. (The stray stack-trace line in `UserRestControllerV1Tests` is a logged expected exception; that class reports 0 failures.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field on the owner response for `POST /api/owners`, set to `\"local\"` when the owner's city is the single most common city among owners existing at registration, otherwise `\"remote\"`.\n\nChanges, following the existing pattern used for the other registration-time computed fields (`membershipNumber`, `customerCode`, `sharesHousehold`, etc.):\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `setLocality`/`getLocality`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a static `locality(Owner, Collection<Owner>)` helper and a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ignore = true)`. It counts owners per city over the population with `id <= owner.id` (cities matched case-insensitively, mirroring the sibling methods), and returns `\"local\"` only when the owner's city count strictly exceeds every other city's count (a tie yields `\"remote\"`, since there is then no *single* most common city). The `id`-bounded population keeps the value stable when read back later, exactly like the other fields.\n- **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST responder) and **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET responder) \u2014 call `dto.setLocality(...)` so the value is present on creation and stable on read-back.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp18Tests` acceptance test (local when a city is dominant, remote for a rare city) passes, along with the full suite.",
